 AI Solution 

The finance industry is one of the key sectors highlighted in the discussion of the 
Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR) and artificial intelligence. Modern banks and 
financial institutions gain a great deal from AI because it automates customer service, 
reduces costs and improves security.

Kwezi Finance is an AI application that targets retail banks in South Africa. Using 
Python-based natural language processing (NLP), the application automatically 
evaluates the enquiries and complaints that customers send through email or chat. It 
determines the urgency of each message, identifies any reported cases of fraud, and 
directs the enquiry to the relevant department.

 Problem Definition 

Retail banks in South Africa receive thousands of customer enquiries every day 
through email, messaging apps and call centres. Conventionally, human operators 
have to read, categorise and route each enquiry to the appropriate department, such 
as the Fraud Department, the Billing Department or the General Enquiries 
Department. This process takes a lot of time, is prone to human error and is very 
expensive.

Most importantly, a customer who reports a stolen bank card or an unauthorised 
transaction waits in the same queue as a customer with a simple question about 
account fees. Delays in identifying and responding to such high-priority issues can 
cause financial losses for both the customer and the bank.
How would solving the problem with AI benefit the organisation and the 
community? The solution is a system that uses NLP to quickly analyse the text of a 
customer message, determine the main issue and assign a priority to it. If a customer 
types “unauthorised transaction”, the AI immediately assigns the case to the Fraud 
Department. This greatly reduces the time taken to respond to urgent financial threats, 
which saves customers’ money. For the bank, it reduces the human labour spent on 
sorting messages.
